{"schema_version": 1, "source_id": "source-04", "embedding_model": "text-embedding-3-small", "dimensions": 512, "records_sha256": "826e5aebc3708d2d5d7f5d7ea86fae2dd55766b755a81e35ca810dbe41ea7012", "records": [{"chunk_id": "source-04/current-policy.pdf:0-1143", "document_id": "source-04/current-policy.pdf", "source_id": "source-04", "section": "Nimbus travel expenses", "start": 0, "end": 1143, "text": "# Nimbus travel expenses\n\nOwner: Finance Operations | Access: workshop-public\n\nVersion: 2026.2. Effective: 2026-09-01. Supersedes previous-policy.html.\n\n## Limits and eligibility\n\n| Category | Domestic / day | International / day |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Meals | USD 45 | USD 85 |\n| Hotel | USD 160 | USD 230 |\n| Ground transport | USD 35 | USD 55 |\n\n## Rule and exception\n\nMeals require itemized receipts. Exception: a lost receipt may be replaced by a signed declaration for one meal costing no more than USD 20 per trip. Alcohol is excluded in all cases.\n\n## Calculation or timing\n\nReimbursement = min(eligible actual expense, applicable daily cap). Meals supplied by an event are not reimbursable.\n\n## Approvals\n\nSubmit within 30 calendar days after the trip ends. Late claims require Finance approval. Customer refunds are governed separately by ../source-06/current-policy.pdf and do not change employee reimbursement limits.\n\nRelated document: operational-notice.png contains a supplemental notice. Check its effective period before applying it.\n\n*Original synthetic workshop content. All organizations and policies here are fictional.*\n", "source_file": "sources/source-04/current-policy.pdf", "metadata": {"title": "Nimbus travel expenses", "version": "2026.2", "effective_date": "2026-09-01", "supersedes": "source-04/previous-policy.html", "owner": "Finance Operations", "access_scope": "workshop-public"}, "vector": [-0.03045654296875, 0.05133056640625, 0.07000732421875, -0.059295654296875, -0.02825927734375, -0.01189422607421875, -0.022491455078125, 0